{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1189923-i-need-help-filling-an-antagonist-npc-roster","id":1189923,"title":"I need help filling an antagonist npc roster","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-27T10:40:29-08:00","id":1189923,"title":"I need help filling an antagonist npc roster","content":"For my first 2nd ed scion game, i'm going with a revival of ymir story. The antagonists will be a conspiracy of like minded (or near enough) beings from multiple mytologies that seek the revival of Ymir for their own reasons.<br /> So far, i have Ice Giants (obviously), Wendigoag and a Yuki-onna businesswoman bankrolling the group.<br /> <br /> Also as a sidequest of sort i have planned for the player to be tasked by Boreas(the greek god of north wind and winter) to find his daugther Khione (goddess of snow) that has eloped with Itztlacoliuhqui (the aztec god of frost and plant freezing to death, i think).<br /> <br /> I also plan for Baba Yaga and Koschei to be important antagonist in the group.<br /> <br /> But i feel, that i am lacking in elements from various other mythologies. I mean, its easy to find cold and winter related figure in norse mythology, but egyptian and the various other african pantheon are a bit more difficult. <br /> <br /> So what i am asking is if some people here have further knowlege on cold/ice/winter related figures and creatures from various mythologies (primarily the pantheons shown in the upcoming core hero book).<br /> <br /> Thank you <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T14:49:05-08:00","id":1190015,"title":"","content":"Now, this is a particular challenge. Frost as a Purview in 1e was overwhelmingly unrepresented in many Pantheons, some cultures just didn't really have a significant notion of it. This makes coming up with antagonists sort of tricky.<br /> <br /> I unfortunately don't really have anybody to offer you for the Tuatha, but I wanted to talk about the Cailleach since you might have a use for her. Now, &quot;The Cailleach,&quot; isn't actually a real entity, is not Irish, and is not a Goddess, the internet will tell you otherwise, but they're mixing up several figures, and it's tainted with some 1970s bad-academia. But, the Scottish Folkloric Winter Hag, Cailleach Bheur, is someone you could use. She is not a Goddess, and isn't one of the Tuatha sadly, so she doesn't quite fit what you are aiming for since she isn't actually part of one of the core Pantheons. However, she would make an awesome Hero antagonist.<br /> <br /> She is a sometimes malignant, sometimes more neutral winter spirit from Scotland (Imported back to Ulster with the transplantation of Scots into Ulster as Cally Berry) who ages backward. She is born as an elderly woman at the start of winter, gets younger the closer to spring it gets. She is reborn every winter, that sort of thing. She is a Hag, sort of like a witch in Scottish folklore, and is appropriately powerful to be about Legend 5-ish. A really big challenge for a Band of Heroes, but someone an individual shiny new Demigod could probably throw down with very successfully. <br /> <br /> Fun thing about her as an antagonist is the Players can't kill her, she will be back every winter, and even if they trap her somehow, she will die naturally as winter ends and will crop back up. They would need to get very clever to deal with her, I would suggest Time Distortion places such as various Otherworlds, or Ryujin's palace, or trapping her in something but leaving it in a realm of perpetual winter so she won't escape through her natural death.<br /> <br /> She would make a good ringleader for your mortal-tier antagonists for sure!<br /> <br /> Oh, and Sacerdos mentioned something about Itztlacoliuhqui that you might be interested in. He has a very important function as a God of Just Punishments.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps! I'm sorry I don't have anything better to offer you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T15:30:49-08:00","id":1190026,"title":"","content":"Poli'ahu from the Polynesian/Hawai'ian pantheon would work if you want cold-themed deities. And don't forget the entire Inue pantheon, such as Sedna, Nanook, and Tulungersak. They are arctic by nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T19:54:40-08:00","id":1190111,"title":"","content":"Apologies, I've been rather occupied today (the baby is handful, what with her tooth emerging and all), so i havent been able to respond promptly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1189923-i-need-help-filling-an-antagonist-npc-roster?p=1190026#post1190026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poli'ahu from the Polynesian/Hawai'ian pantheon would work if you want cold-themed deities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, i honestly wouldn't have expected the Polynesian/Hawai'ian pantheon to have a cold-themed divinity<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1189923-i-need-help-filling-an-antagonist-npc-roster?p=1190026#post1190026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't forget the entire Inue pantheon, such as Sedna, Nanook, and Tulungersak. They are arctic by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan with the Inue pantheon was that at Demigod level the players will need to figure out a way to protect themselves against supernatural cold. And they will have to contact the Inue pantheon and in exchange to some help they will be given a protection of sort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1189923-i-need-help-filling-an-antagonist-npc-roster?p=1190015#post1190015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, this is a particular challenge. Frost as a Purview in 1e was overwhelmingly unrepresented in many Pantheons, some cultures just didn't really have a significant notion of it. This makes coming up with antagonists sort of tricky.<br /> <br /> I unfortunately don't really have anybody to offer you for the Tuatha, but I wanted to talk about the Cailleach since you might have a use for her. Now, &quot;The Cailleach,&quot; isn't actually a real entity, is not Irish, and is not a Goddess, the internet will tell you otherwise, but they're mixing up several figures, and it's tainted with some 1970s bad-academia. But, the Scottish Folkloric Winter Hag, Cailleach Bheur, is someone you could use. She is not a Goddess, and isn't one of the Tuatha sadly, so she doesn't quite fit what you are aiming for since she isn't actually part of one of the core Pantheons. However, she would make an awesome Hero antagonist.<br /> <br /> She is a sometimes malignant, sometimes more neutral winter spirit from Scotland (Imported back to Ulster with the transplantation of Scots into Ulster as Cally Berry) who ages backward. She is born as an elderly woman at the start of winter, gets younger the closer to spring it gets. She is reborn every winter, that sort of thing. She is a Hag, sort of like a witch in Scottish folklore, and is appropriately powerful to be about Legend 5-ish. A really big challenge for a Band of Heroes, but someone an individual shiny new Demigod could probably throw down with very successfully.<br /> <br /> Fun thing about her as an antagonist is the Players can't kill her, she will be back every winter, and even if they trap her somehow, she will die naturally as winter ends and will crop back up. They would need to get very clever to deal with her, I would suggest Time Distortion places such as various Otherworlds, or Ryujin's palace, or trapping her in something but leaving it in a realm of perpetual winter so she won't escape through her natural death.<br /> <br /> She would make a good ringleader for your mortal-tier antagonists for sure!<br /> <br /> Oh, and Sacerdos mentioned something about Itztlacoliuhqui that you might be interested in. He has a very important function as a God of Just Punishments.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps! I'm sorry I don't have anything better to offer you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh that is interesting. It explains why i've found so little information on a cold/winter based god/ess or monster despite the fact that the Irish pantheon would have a few myth dealing with cold and winter. At least more than say the egyptian pantheon which i completely understand them not having anything related to cold/winter.<br /> <br /> But i will definitively look into the Cailleach Bheur, i am a bit afraid that she steps on the Baba Yaga toes. But i could work if i put her up as a lieutenant of Baba Yaga that the player meets at mortal/hero level. <br /> <br /> Anyway, amazing help so far. You've given much to research. Thank you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T23:50:54-08:00","id":1190163,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that 2E is following the &quot;all myths are real&quot; model rather than just deities, so not-quite-religious figures like Jack Frost, Grandfather Frost, the Great Winter General, and other non-godly personifications of winter might be worth considering. They're often less directly antagonistic than what it sounds like you're looking for, though. Some might serve better as middle powered mentors than antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T02:39:11-08:00","id":1190183,"title":"","content":"As for winter gods there is Tawiscara from the Orenda. He basically created winter to undo his brother's creations and kidnapped all the animals and sealed them in a cave. I also remember reading somewhere that he tried to connect the land of famine monsters with the world but the singing of the bluebird and Iosheka scared him away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T02:56:48-08:00","id":1190185,"title":"","content":"Pomola of the Wabanaki Pantheon and Hahhima of the Shiunesh are both Titans/Antagonist deities that I feel would fit your criteria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:21:23-08:00","id":1190530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1189923-i-need-help-filling-an-antagonist-npc-roster?p=1190163#post1190163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that 2E is following the &quot;all myths are real&quot; model rather than just deities, so not-quite-religious figures like Jack Frost, Grandfather Frost, the Great Winter General, and other non-godly personifications of winter might be worth considering. They're often less directly antagonistic than what it sounds like you're looking for, though. Some might serve better as middle powered mentors than antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, quite interesting, i hadn't thought of using the more 'fairy tales' myth. <br /> Now i'm thinking of Santa Claus (as one of Odin's mantles) ask the player to save Jack Frost who has been corrupted by the conspiracy somehow. It might make for a nice little christmas game even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T12:35:21-08:00","id":1191082,"title":"","content":"Would <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Frost_(1997_film)\" target=\"_blank\">psychotic killer snowmen</a> titan-spawn be too ludicrous?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T13:25:30-08:00","id":1191102,"title":"","content":"The Inuit have a crazy number of monsters that would make good Titanspawn, too many to list here. The Mahaha, Adlet, Ijiraq, Tizheruk, Ikuutayuuq, Akhlut, A-Mi-Kuk, and Paija are a few to look into, but there's many more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T00:26:18-08:00","id":1192547,"title":"","content":"Ymir may not just be an ice giant only. Why not other purviews so other pantheons could be related to him? Health, water, earth? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T16:32:04-08:00","id":1193352,"title":"","content":"Two ways to bring in warm-weather pantheons:<br /> Frost as weapon against fire (e.g., who wants to take Re down a peg?)<br /> Frost as incentive for fire worship (e.g., Hestia is feeling under-appreciated and thinks a new ice age would really drive home the importance of the hearth)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","name":"zilaenor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T16:37:41-08:00","id":1193355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zilaenor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1189923-i-need-help-filling-an-antagonist-npc-roster?p=1193352#post1193352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two ways to bring in warm-weather pantheons:<br /> Frost as weapon against fire (e.g., who wants to take Re down a peg?)<br /> Frost as incentive for fire worship (e.g., Hestia is feeling under-appreciated and thinks a new ice age would really drive home the importance of the hearth)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, i like this.<br /> Using fire/warmth related enemies could also allow for using the more friendly frost related entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}